name w2-04-loaded
timeout 6700
time 1981-06-07T12:55:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W2, SORTIE 4 OF 10 - OSIRAK 1981 (OPERATION OPERA): REACH, NOT COMBAT.
# THE SAME RIDE UNDER THE WAR LOAD. WHAT TWO Mk-84 COST IN KILOMETRES.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w2-osirak.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w2-03-radius.fbm. ONE FACT DIFFERS - the two `set store` lines. Same spawn, same leg,
# same altitude, same commanded speed, same internal fuel, SAME OBJECTIVES. It is in turn the
# control of w2-05-tanks.fbm (ONE fact: two tank370 on the plumbed stations 4 and 6). Callsigns are
# disjoint across all three, per O4's rule: the store carry is keyed by callsign.
#
# THE ANCHOR: the package flew "over 1,600 km" for the round trip and was "near the limit of its
# range"; the external tanks were exhausted en route and jettisoned over the Saudi desert [T4]. The
# same source's own straight-line figure is ~1,090 km each way, which does not agree with its own
# round-trip number; MEASURED between the two coordinates the source itself gives (Etzion 29.94/34.87,
# Al-Tuwaitha 33.20/44.52) the great circle is 982.9 km each way, 1,965.9 km out and back [DERIVED].
# ALL THREE FIGURES ARE CARRIED. The campaign compares its measured radius against all of them and
# averages none.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DO THE STORES COST IN RADIUS? The spec asks it about the carriage
# penalty already measured in mass and Mach (+2,000 lb, Mach 1.416 -> 1.364 for four Mk-82) and says
# plainly what this file is for: "this converts it into kilometres". THE LADDER WAS FLOWN FIRST, as an
# attribution run outside the ten (campaign file §State); one straight leg at 240 m / 400 kt /
# `fuel_int_pct 100` to fuel exhaustion, one configuration per row:
#   clean                            FLAMEOUT AT 1,492.6 km, 4.6708 lb/km  -> radius 746.3 km
#   2 x Mk-84 (THIS FILE)            FLAMEOUT AT 1,162.3 km, 5.9984 lb/km  -> radius 581.2 km
#   -> THE WAR LOAD COSTS 330.3 km, 22.1 % OF THE CLEAN RANGE [DERIVED, 1 - 1162.3/1492.6], on two
#      stores weighing 4,078 lb and adding 2 x 1.0261 ft^2 of drag area
# The leg below is unchanged from the control: 671.7 km out and back, 90 % of the CLEAN radius. That
# is deliberate - the two runs have to fly the same ground for the fuel difference to mean anything,
# and 1,343.4 km is 115.6 % of this jet's own radius. IT IS NOT EXPECTED TO GET HOME.
# WHAT THE NUMBER IS NOT, STATED BEFORE IT IS READ. This jet spawns IN THE AIR at cruise altitude and
# cruise speed. The anchor's aircraft started their engines, taxied, took off and climbed on the same
# fuel, and FlightBox models none of that: EVERY W2 RANGE NUMBER IS AN UPPER BOUND on the flyable
# radius, and the direction of the error is known and one-sided.
#
# THE ARENA: the raid's own outbound track from Etzion AB 29.94000 34.87000 [T4, approximate] on
# bearing 068.37 deg, out to the 671.7 km turn point and back to Etzion. Scale: 1 deg lat = 111,320 m,
# 1 deg lon at 31.570 N = 94,845 m [DERIVED].
#   `w2pit`  target_soft  32.16405 41.41736 - a desert installation at the turn point (campaign rule 3)
#
# WHY THIS FILE STILL DECLARES NO `kill` OBJECTIVE, AND WHY THAT IS THE DISCIPLINED CHOICE. Its
# control w2-03 carries nothing to attack with, so a `kill` objective here would make the two runs
# differ in TWO things - the stores AND the verdict - and neither difference could then be attributed.
# The objectives are identical in all three files of this ladder; the kill is read out of
# `UNIT_RESULT` beside the fuel.
# THE SIX STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES, in short form (full text in w2-01-dome.fbm):
#   1. `C5` half closed - the tank exists and is NOT on this jet (that is w2-05); AERIAL REFUELLING
#      IS NOT BUILT, so nothing in this campaign says what a tanker would have been worth.
#   2. `C20` open, `--elev const`, 0 m plane; the real ground under this route is 42.83-1,599.22 m
#      (MEASURED, listed in w2-02-ingress.fbm). Etzion itself is at 523.59 m, so this jet flies its
#      whole ride 283.59 m BELOW its own airfield.
#   3. `C10` - level laydown. This jet carries two Mk-84 and has no aim point on its route: the
#      stores are here for their MASS AND DRAG, which is the whole subject, and nothing is released.
#   4/5/6 - no F-15, `FirstFlightKo`, W1's fixed point: all irrelevant, this is a single jet alone.
#
# READING RULE (binding): the exit code is NOT the measurement. Read, in this order: (1) `fuelLbs` in
# the LAST telemetry row - the campaign contract §2 requires every mission to report it and this is the
# file it was written for, (2) whether both `nav WP_REACHED` lines appear, (3) the ground distance
# flown. A run that lands with reserve to spare has not tested the thing this raid was about; a run
# that does not get home has answered the campaign's central question in the negative.

# MEASURED (fingerprint 42c542e4ec72c306, exit 2): THE WAR LOAD DOES NOT GET HOME.
#   the leg       `nav WP_REACHED idx=0` at t=3,261.2 s - the SAME turn point at the SAME tick as the
#                 clean control, to 0.1 s. The second waypoint is never reached
#   the end       `monitor KO ... reason=STRUCTURE_CONTACT` at t=5,751.6 s at 30.5283/36.6020,
#                 179.0 km SHORT of Etzion, fuel 0.0 lb. Exit 2 is the CORRECT outcome and it is the
#                 campaign's central negative result
#   the price     two 2,039 lb stores are worth 330.3 km of clean range, 22.1 % (A1: 1,162.3 km of
#                 flameout distance against 1,492.6 clean) and +1.3276 lb/km of specific consumption
#   Read beside w2-03-radius.fbm (its control) and w2-05-tanks.fbm (one further lever).

unit w2rad4
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 29.94000 34.87000 240 68.4 400        # Etzion AB, on the raid's own outbound bearing
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100                        # 6,972 lb internal - the SAME internal load as w2-03
  set store 3 mk84                            # THE ONE FACT: the raid's own war load, two Mk-84 ...
  set store 7 mk84                            # ... and nothing else about this jet differs
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 32.16405 41.41736 240 400                # THE TURN POINT: 671.7 km out = 90 % of the measured radius
  wp 29.94000 34.87000 240 400                # home, the same 671.7 km back
  objective waypoints
  objective survive

unit w2pit4
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 32.16405 41.41736 ground 68.4 0
